A||||1||ezsurf||Replacement Clutch Pedal
Z||000000||ezsurf||08-02-99||01:53 PM||||<br>Where can I get the steel replacement clutch pedal?  The clutch doesn't seem to want to fully engage.  It is most noticable in reverse.  If this doesn't fix the problem, the only other thing I know to do is bleed the system again.  Unless someone has another idea.
Z||000001||Bruce||08-02-99||05:59 PM||||According to V8 Archie, you can order the pedal thru any Pontiac Dealership. It's part #10066423, and costs around $32.75. Go to www.v8archie/arch6.htm for a complete explanation of the installation.<br>You might also check the linkage bolts that are to the left of the engine. Mine wore down and it was difficult to shift into third and reverse. I had the bolts adjusted (i.e. turned about 180 degrees, the linkage lubricated, and the problem was solved
